es together, in one step.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Kilometres: keep <b class="gd-ui">Use the defaults</b> (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car&#39;s class), or choose <b class="gd-ui">Custom for this car</b> and type them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rates</b>.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Rate</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Daily rate</td><td>A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday</td></tr><tr><td>Weekend rate</td><td>A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly rate</td><td>The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly rate</td><td>The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (the tiers there), <b class="gd-ui">Off for this car</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Its own tiers</b> (a table like the one in Program settings). Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b>, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><div>Coming soon: The Tracker card on a car says &quot;Coming soon&quot;: live location, the remote immobilize request and mileage from the tracker need the tracker company&#39;s connection first.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-listing-pipeline" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The listing pipeline</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the pipeline&#39;s progress.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> to begin one for a car that has none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car to review it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:53.5%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:87.2%;top:21.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-review-a-listing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review a listing</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pipeline shows each step done, such as photo sizes, copy draft and backgrounds.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b>. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself from the car&#39;s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1100"><img src="/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1100"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.6%;top:16.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86.1%;top:47.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cover-the-licence-plate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cover the licence plate</h2><p class="gd-p">On each public photo press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b>. The editor opens.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The editor suggests a box over the plate. Check it. <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b> asks again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under Cover the plate with, choose <b class="gd-ui">A CarmaCars plate</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Pixelation</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Blur</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Clear the boxes</b> starts over.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? Press <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:690/703"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="690" height="703"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:42.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:49.6%;top:29.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.3%;top:77.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.1%;top:91.2%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press <b class="gd-ui">Set rates and publish</b>. The daily rate is filled in (the car&#39;s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On the car itself, the Listing tab has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">From a listing review: press <b class="gd-ui">Approve and publish</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approve, publish later</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with what to fix.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show &quot;Plate not checked&quot; on such photos.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-listing-without-photos-yet-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A listing without photos yet: sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car&#39;s details.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car page and the car&#39;s card show a sample photo, captioned &quot;Sample photo&quot;, so renters know it is not this car. Staff see &quot;Using sample photos&quot; on the car and in Listings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sample photos</b>. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> a photo you no longer want.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:26.8%;top:28.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish-now-and-new-cars-published-by-themselves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now, and new cars published by themselves</h2><p class="gd-p">Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Publish new cars automatically</b> (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner&#39;s application is approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-checklist-what-is-still-open-on-a-listed-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The checklist: what is still open on a listed car</h2><p class="gd-p">Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car&#39;s Listing tab and after Publish now.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Paperwork</td><td>Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance</td><td>Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over</td></tr><tr><td>Details</td><td>Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing</td></tr><tr><td>Photos</td><td>No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is</td></tr><tr><td>No VIN yet</td><td>A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it</td></tr><tr><td>Possible duplicate</td><td>An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site</td></tr><tr><td>Owner terms</td><td>The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner&#39;s terms or the standard grid</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-fleet-policy-rule-at-handover" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The fleet policy rule at handover</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.</li><li>The handover refuses the car until the insurer&#39;s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.</li><li>Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cars-on-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cars on sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> ends with <b class="gd-ui">Cars on sample photos</b>: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-out and check-in photos field staff take).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Where a handover photographed the car, press <b class="gd-ui">Use the handover photos</b>. They go into the car&#39;s listing as if taken on the capture screen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: the studio editor puts the car on the CarmaCars backdrop, then the listing waits for your review like any other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> and take them.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The studio editor uses Cloudflare image transformations (5,000 a month included). Settings &gt; Usage counts them.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-s-registration-and-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s registration and documents</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then <b class="gd-ui">Owner, documents, tracker</b>. The <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b> card:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Correct the <b class="gd-ui">VIN</b> (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the <b class="gd-ui">Year</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Body style</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type the <b class="gd-ui">Ontario permit number</b> and the date the <b class="gd-ui">Plate sticker expires</b>. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>, choose the kind (<b class="gd-ui">Ownership permit</b>, Safety Standards Certificate, owner&#39;s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press <b class="gd-ui">Upload</b>. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner&#39;s checklist.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">For the <b class="gd-ui">Safety Standards Certificate</b>, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under <b class="gd-ui">Documents (optional)</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-added-under-the-wrong-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car added under the wrong owner</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Who supplies the car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Move to another owner</b>. Choose the owner, or <b class="gd-ui">CarmaCars (owner not known yet)</b>: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The car&#39;s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.</li><li>It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand', 'chapter', 'fleet-and-listings', 'A car comes from one of three places: a program owner, CarmaCars itself, or a partner rental company. You add cars and rentals by hand, retire cars, and delete cars that were added by mistake.

## Add a car

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then **Add a car**. Start with the VIN: everything else about the car comes from it.

1. Type or paste the VIN. At the 17th character the car is looked up: one line shows the year, make, model, trim, body, seats, doors, fuel, drive, gearbox and engine. Press Edit only if something is wrong.
2. When the VIN fits several trims, the form asks which trim it is: press the one on the car''s papers or badge, or **Not sure** (Admin > Today asks again).
3. No VIN at hand? Press **No VIN at hand? Add the car by its plate** and choose the year, make and model from the lists. The VIN can be added later; the details fill in then.
4. Tap the colour (it is not in the VIN). Leave it empty and it is read from the cover photo once the car has one.
5. Check the class. It is set from the make, model, body and age (a 2016 Porsche Macan is Premium, an SUV is SUV) and the line under it says why. Change it if it is wrong.
6. Choose who supplies it: **A program owner''s car** (choose the owner; the car starts its onboarding), **CarmaCars-owned (company fleet)** (no owner; all of its revenue is CarmaCars'') or **A partner rental company''s car** (choose the partner; leave the commission empty to use the partner''s).
7. The daily rate is filled in from similar cars, else the class. Keep it, change it, or empty it and set the rates later on the car''s Rates tab. Press **Add the car**.

> Tip: The title, description and features are written by themselves right after the car is added, from the VIN details. Change any of them on the car''s listing; a field you change is kept.

> Good to know: Every car gets a fleet number and its standard settings the moment it is added: a complete rate card (the daily rate you typed or the suggested one, weekend, weekly and monthly from it, the kilometres a day, the extra kilometre rate, the deposit and the delivery and pickup fee of its class) and drivers 18 to 20 allowed. Each value set this way says (Set automatically) on the car''s Overview and Rates tab until you change it. The defaults come from Settings: Program and Fee defaults.

> Tip: A VIN that does not add up (one character misread) shows a warning; you can still save it. A VIN the decoder cannot read asks only the year, make and model and never stops you: the details fill in when it is read later. The duplicate check runs as for every car: a VIN only once, a plate on one active car, and a likely twin waits for you in Similar cars before it is published.

The gearbox comes from the government''s fuel economy data for the model when it has one gearbox for it, or from the VIN when the VIN states it. Seats come from the VIN, or the usual number for the body (4 for a coupe or convertible, 5 for a sedan, SUV or hatchback). When either is not certain, Admin > Today shows **Confirm gearbox and seats**: press the gearbox and the number of seats, then **Save**. A car whose VIN fits several trims shows **Pick the trim** there: press the right one. Either way the title, description and search text are written again.

On a car''s page, **Who supplies the car** shows the supplier and the commission, and changes them. Vehicles filters by supply type.

## Partners

**People** > **Partners**. Partner rental companies whose cars we rent out on commission.

1. Press **Add a partner**: business and legal name, contacts, HST number, commission and insurance with its expiry date.
2. Open a partner for its cars, bookings, statements, payouts and documents. A warning shows when its insurance expires soon, and Staff tasks gets a reminder (Program settings sets how many days before).
3. Banking (Admins only): **Save the payout account** for the account we pay the partner into. The account number is stored encrypted. Press **Verify** once checked.
4. Portal: **Invite to the owner portal** gives the partner the owner portal with its cars, bookings, statements and the partner agreement, filled in and signed on screen in three taps.
5. Signed on paper? Press **Print the partner agreement**, then record the signed scan under Record a paper signature.

## A partner fleet on its own rates

Some partners send a price sheet of their own rates instead of sharing what the renter pays. 01 Motors works this way: its whole fleet is on the site, and staff manage its cars (it has no portal sign-in yet; add its email on the partner page and invite it later).

1. **People** > **Partners** > the partner. **Pricing** shows how it is paid: the renter pays the partner''s sheet rate plus the markup (10% unless you set another), rounded to the nearest dollar; CarmaCars keeps the markup plus its cut (20% of the sheet rate); the partner is owed the rest of its sheet rate. Press **Edit pricing** to change the markup, the cut or the basis for every car at once.
2. **Cars** lists each car with its sheet rates a day (1 to 2 days, 3 or more, 7 or more) and the renter''s rates. Press **Edit** on a car to change a negotiated rate, give that car its own markup or cut, mark it **Insurance included** or **No credit card needed**, or confirm its model year. The renter''s rates change at once.
3. The site shows these cars with their tiers (1 to 2 days, 3 to 6 days, 7 days or more) and "Guideline rates; final price confirmed after review". A car with insurance included needs no coverage choice from the renter (coverage option 4, confirmed by itself); a car with no credit card needed takes a debit card for the payment and the deposit. The deposit, the licence and identity checks and the ages stay the same.
4. The price sheet has no years, VINs or plates. Until you confirm the year, the site leaves it out and says "Year confirmed when you book"; an offer waits until the year is confirmed (Edit on the car, Model year). Add the plate and the VIN on the car''s page before its first handover.
5. Real photos: open the car (its name in Cars), **Photos**, and add them. Once approved they replace the eight studio stand-ins.

> Good to know: The partner''s monthly statement shows each rental at the sheet rate, the cut and the payout; never what the renter paid. A refund lowers the partner''s share in proportion; a discount CarmaCars gives comes out of the markup.

## A partner''s CRM (01 Motors'' GoHighLevel)

**Settings**, the **Partners** tile, then the partner (or **CRM link** on the partner''s page). Their CRM gets our cars, kept up to date, and their cars come to us.

1. Ask the partner for a Private Integration token and their location ID (the box **What 01 Motors gives us** on the page says exactly what to create and which scopes to tick). Paste both and press **Connect**. The token goes to the vault; the page only ever shows its last four characters.
2. Connect tests the link (their location, objects, products and pipelines) and runs the first sync. After that it runs by itself every 15 minutes, and within five minutes of a change to a car, a rate, a photo, a booking or a block. **Test connection** and **Run sync now** do it at once.
3. **What 01 Motors sees**: CarmaCars'' own cars and program owners'' cars that are on the site, with rates, the next 60 days and photos, as records of a "CarmaCars Vehicles" object in their CRM (or as products when their plan has no custom objects). Partner cars are never sent: not theirs, not another partner''s. Press **Change what we share** to leave out program owners'' cars, rates, availability or photos.
4. **Partner price**: the site''s rates, or the site''s rates less (or plus) a percentage, to the nearest dollar.
5. **Their cars coming in**: name the object in their CRM that holds their cars (Test connection lists them), or their feed address. Each of their cars is matched to their car here, or added as their partner car (it waits off the site unless you choose otherwise), with their rates as its sheet rates, their booked dates as calendar blocks and their photos for a car with none. A car that waits shows **Add as their car**, **Link** or **Set aside**.
6. **Leads both ways** (off until you turn it on): requests for their cars, and requests that came through their booking links, become contacts and opportunities in the pipeline stage you choose; an opportunity they move to the stage you name becomes a lead in **Leads**.
7. **Feed, widget and booking links**: a JSON or CSV feed and a widget for their GoHighLevel funnels and sites (copy the iframe), and booking links carmacars.ca/p/01-motors/<car> that mark the request as theirs for 30 days. **New key** ends the old feed and widget addresses at once.

> Good to know: A link that has failed for an hour shows on Admin > Today. Disconnect deletes the token from the vault; what is already in their CRM stays there.

## Add a rental by hand

**Bookings** > **Add a rental**. For phone, walk-in, Turo, partner and insurer bookings, the owner using their own car, and placeholders: a rental already agreed. To send an offer instead, use Send an offer.

1. Standing with the renter at pickup? Press **Start at pickup**: type the renter''s name and phone, choose the car, type the kilometres and the fuel, and press **Hold the car and finish later**. The pickup is now; the car is held for 2 hours (renewed while you work on it) and you get a task to finish the rental.
2. Nothing is required to save: the form is saved as a draft as you type (**Save draft** saves at once). Unfinished rentals, on Bookings and on this page, lists every draft with who started it, when, and what is still missing; Finish it opens it where it was left, on any device. Tick Hold the car while I finish to keep the car off the calendar while you type (2 hours, renewed as you save). Discard drops it and frees the car.
3. Quick start sets the usual choices in one tap: **Phone**, **Walk-in**, **Turo or another platform**, **Insurance replacement**, **Owner using own car** or **Placeholder**.
4. Choose the car and the dates. The calendar and the price are checked by themselves: clashes with other bookings and the cleaning time after each trip. An Admin may book over a clash with a reason.
5. The dates decide the case, shown under them (nothing to tick): a pickup ahead is an upcoming rental, handed over at pickup as usual. A pickup already passed with the return ahead is a rental already underway: it is recorded as on trip from the pickup you enter, on any active car (even one closed to public bookings), and anything a handover checks that is still missing (signature, licence check, coverage proof, deposit, condition report, insurance) becomes a task. A return already passed is a rental that has ended: kept as completed, paid another way or unpaid.
6. Find the renter by name, email or phone, or add a new one: name, email, phone, date of birth and licence. Add any other drivers.
7. We deliver it, or we pick it up: pick the address from the suggestions and its distance from our location prices the delivery (shown under the address), as on Send an offer.
8. Check the price: every line of the price can be changed where it stands. Type a new amount in the line (the rental charge for the trip or a rate a day, the young driver fee, the Protection Plan, delivery, each add-on, the deposit, the kilometres a day); HST and the total follow. Add a line from the list or a charge of its own; Remove takes a fee off. The (i) beside each line says what it is and how it is worked out. One optional reason covers all the changes. At the top of the price, Amounts I type: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter paid for each line ("$270 after tax for the rental, $50 for the Protection Plan"): each is worked back to its amount before tax, and a line without HST stays as typed. The choice is remembered on this device. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out so the total is exactly that, to the cent, and the line under it shows each line before tax. The total shown is the total that is saved; if they ever differ, it says by how much before you save.
9. Any length: the dates may run past 30 days (up to the staff limit in Program settings, 730 days by default). From 30 days the rental charge is the monthly rate for each 30 days, and the monthly periods are listed. On the booking, Monthly periods shows each period: its share, and its own version of the agreement (CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s), sent to the renter to sign a few days before it starts (Program settings: long_rental_agreement_lead_days, 3 by default), with what is due for it on the renter''s Balance due. With Program settings, Charge the saved card for each period, on, that share is charged to the saved card when the agreement goes out (the renter gets the receipt; a declined or missing card gives Finance a task).
10. A car whose listing is not finished (a draft listing, onboarding, no photos or no rates yet) can be rented at once: it shows Listing not finished in the car list and stays off the public site. With no rates yet, type the rental charge for the whole rental and the reason.
11. An owner''s car that is not on the fleet insurance policy yet: only an Admin adds its rentals, and ticks I checked that this car is insured for this rental. An owner''s car needs its terms (Revenue Share) first. The handover still needs the car on the fleet policy: press **Insurer confirmed** once the insurer confirms it.
12. Insurer billed later (or the Insurance replacement quick start): choose the insurer (Not listed: type its name, and it is added to the list), the claim number, the adjuster, the days and the daily rate authorized, the provisional end, and whether the insurer pays everything or the rental only. The booking is billed to the insurer; the renter owes only what it does not cover. The daily rate authorized is filled from the insurer''s rate sheet for the car (Insurance replacements: rates and billing); a different rate needs the reason. Charges to the insurer: type the rate a day of VLF, LDW, T&LDW, PAP/PEC or Waiver Saver when the insurer authorized them (Insurance replacements: rates and billing).
13. The rent is paid by: e-Transfer or cash (received), card on file (charged when the renter signs), payment link, platform payout (Turo), insurer billed later, cheque, bank transfer, or unpaid. Paid in parts (some cash, some e-Transfer): press **Add another payment (paid in parts)** and type each amount. Then the deposit, its own way: card hold, cash, e-Transfer (with its reference and date) or no deposit.
14. Before you save checks it all in one box: the renter, the car, the days, the total, what was received and what is still to collect, the deposit (or No deposit) and the agreement.
15. The rental agreement: Send it to sign online, or Already signed on paper (a task asks for the scan). The calendar: untick Blocks the car''s calendar for an insurance replacement with dates not known yet, with the reason.
16. Tick **Do not email the renter** if they should not get the confirmation. Press **Add the rental**.

> Tip: The rental is on the calendars at once (a payment link waits for the payment). The renter signs the rental agreement in their portal, or on paper and you record it. With the saved card, nothing is charged when you add the rental: the card is charged when the renter presses Accept and sign, and until then the rental is awaiting signature. On the booking, **Verified in person** records a licence checked at the counter. A rental already underway can be paid by payment link (the renter signs, then pays from their booking) or the saved card, like an upcoming one.

## Retire or delete a car

**Cars** > **Retire or delete**, or the car''s own page.

1. **Retire this car** takes the car off the site and the calendars and keeps every record. It needs no future confirmed booking. **Restore** brings it back.
2. **Delete this car** removes a car added by mistake, with its photos. Only a car with nothing tied to money (no confirmed or paid booking, payment, statement, toll or damage). Type the plate or the name to confirm.
3. Booking requests that never confirmed and never took money (requested, offered, declined, expired) do not stop a delete. The confirmation lists them; they are removed with the car and a copy is kept. The renters stay on file.
4. On the same page, **Delete all sample cars** deletes every sample car that meets the rule at once, with its requests. Type DELETE SAMPLE CARS to confirm; the ones kept show why, with the booking numbers.

## Sample cars on the site

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, or **Settings** > **Site**. The 20 example cars the site started with, so the fleet never looks empty while the real cars are listed.

1. **Hide sample cars** asks first ("Hide all 20 sample cars from the site?"); press **Hide them** to take every sample car off the site at once, or **Keep them**. Nothing else stops it: not an enquiry, not an old request.
2. **Show sample cars** puts the 20 back, with their photos and rates. Ones that were deleted are made again.
3. On the site each one is marked "Example car". They never appear in search engines or the sitemap.
4. A request on a sample car is never a booking. When the person picks dates, the car page and the request form show a real car free for them (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price) with one tap to switch to it. If they keep the sample car, it becomes an enquiry (number EQ-1001 and up) and customer service gets the task Suggest a similar real car, naming the free real car.

> Tip: Hide the sample cars once enough real cars are on the site. Delete all sample cars removes them for good.

## Why a car is not on the site yet

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, the card Not on the site yet.

1. Every real car that is not on the site is listed with its next step first: the rates, Publish now, the listing review.
2. The same car is a line on To do with **Set rates and publish**. The car comes off both once it is on the site.
3. A car without photos is marked sample photos: once listed it shows a sample photo until its real photos are approved.

## Placeholder bookings

A placeholder is a booking held for an insurer, or as a hold, next to the real rental on the same car.

1. On **Add a rental**, press **Placeholder** (Admins). It never blocks the calendar, is never handed over, sends the renter nothing, earns no commission and is left off the Live map. The owner sees only that the car is unavailable. Type what it is for, or leave it empty.
2. Enter the real rental as usual, even for the same days: it blocks the car, and tolls, tickets and damage go to it.
3. A booking made another way can become one: on the booking, **More actions** > **Mark as a placeholder**. Not once money was taken or the car went out. **Make it a real booking** undoes it; then turn the calendar switch on if it should hold the car.
4. On the booking, **Competing for these dates** (and **Also on this car for these dates** once booked) lists everything else on the car for those days and says which one keeps it off the car. A placeholder never counts.

## Tolls when two rentals overlap

Bookings held for an insurer and other placeholders are never matched to a toll. When two real rentals overlap the toll time, nobody is charged automatically: the toll waits in the work queue under Two rentals, with both bookings, and you choose who pays.
